BACKGROUND

In 2024, Partap Singh, an illegal alien from India, caused a multi-car pileup while driving a commercial 18-wheeler in California. Even though he was an illegal alien, California still issued Singh a Commercial Driver’s License (CDL), allowing him to operate the semi-truck. The crash resulted in five-year-old Dalilah Coleman suffering life-altering injuries. Sadly, Dalilah is not the only American who has been killed or injured by illegal aliens operating commercial vehicles after sanctuary states issued them CDLs.

